Rust Util local modifications, 2026-11-26

Tesseract.js 6.0.1 is distributed under Apache License 2.0; see LICENSE.md.
The vendored tesseract.min.js differs from the upstream package in two places:
1. Initialization-chain failures reject the createWorker promise and terminate the worker instead of being swallowed.
2. The optional onWorker callback exposes the native worker immediately after creation, allowing cancellation during initialization.

scripts/vendor-ocr.py applies both exact, version-checked replacements reproducibly and records resulting SHA-256 checksums in manifest.json.
Other bundled OCR files are not modified. The local OCR supervisor in assets/ocr.js imposes a 120-second deadline and releases native workers on cancellation, success and failure.
